<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/monopole.rs. std only. Maximal abelian gauge for SU(2): functional mean(a0^2 + a3^2 - a1^2 - a2^2); per site X = sum_mu [U s3 U^dagger + U(x-mu)^dagger s3 U(x-mu)] as a 3-vector, gauge rotation taking it to +z (choose the half-angle sign that lands closest to +z), over-relaxation by raising to the power omega; checkerboard over site parity via Lattice::gauge_transform; fix_mag(l, omega, tol, max) returns (functional, sweeps). abelian_angles: arg(a0 + i a3). DeGrand-Toussaint: plaquette_integers n_p from theta_p = [theta_p] + 2 pi n_p, [.] in (-pi, pi]; cube_charge at x for a<b<c = -(boundary sum +P_bc(x+a) - P_bc(x) - P_ac(x+b) + P_ac(x) + P_ab(x+c) - P_ab(x)); monopole_density = mean |m| over 3-cubes. Independent tests in tests/monopole.rs: charges invariant under U(1) gauge transformations with re-wrapping; zero net charge in closed 3-slices; none on the cold configuration; MAG functional nondecreasing per sweep (omega = 1), plaquette unchanged, convergence with omega = 1.7. examples/monopole_scan: density against beta for su2 (after MAG) and u1 (direct).
